{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And if there be in a man a sin worthy of death.</b> The juxtaposition of the passages teaches: if his father and mother spare him, the end is that he will turn to evil ways and commit transgressions and be liable to the death penalty in court (see Tanḥuma)." "<b>And you hang him on a tree.</b> Our Rabbis said: all who are stoned are hanged, as it is said ״כִּי קִלְלַת אֱלֹהִים תָּלוּי״, and one who blasphemes HaShem [is punished] by stoning (Sanhedrin 45)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:54.976548374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}